<div class="sec" id="s1">
  <div class="num">01</div>
  <h2>What these tools do</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    An agent is an AI that can act on your computer, not only answer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Claude chat gives you words to work with. Claude Code is a program from
    Anthropic that can read files, change them and run commands: typed
    instructions to your computer. What you ask an AI to do is called a prompt.
  </p>
  <p>
    For your first website, use the <a href="#s5">supplied build request</a>.
    For your own projects, Claude chat can help you
    <a href="#s4">write a clear request</a> before you give it to Claude Code. Your
    browser, the app you use to visit websites, is where you check the result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delta is a separate app for working with agents and reviewing their changes.
    It has different account requirements and fewer safety controls. Its
    <a href="/delta/index.html">optional assisted follow-up</a> is not part of this
    first build.
  </p>
  <p>
    You do not have to understand every line of code. You do have to understand
    what the agent says it is going to change, and check the result yourself. A
    confident explanation and a working page are different things.
  </p>
</div>
